      },
      "files": {
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n  <title>Live Weather Data</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\" />\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"page\">\n    <section class=\"weather-card\">\n      <div class=\"header\">\n        <p class=\"label\">Live Weather</p>\n        <h1 id=\"cityName\">San Francisco, CA</h1>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"forecast\">\n        <p id=\"description\">Loading forecast...</p>\n        <p id=\"tempMain\">--</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"details\">\n        <p>Chance of Rain: <strong id=\"rainChance\">--</strong></p>\n        <p>Wind: <strong id=\"wind\">--</strong></p>\n      </div>\n\n      <button id=\"refreshButton\">Refresh Forecast</button>\n    </section>\n  </main>\n\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "3": {
          "id": "3",
          "name": "styles.css",
          "language": "css",
          "contents": "body {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n  background: #eef4f8;\n  color: #1f2d3d;\n}\n\n.page {\n  min-height: 100vh;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  padding: 24px;\n}\n\n.weather-card {\n  width: 100%;\n  max-width: 420px;\n  background: white;\n  border-radius: 18px;\n  padding: 28px;\n  box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);\n}\n\n.header {\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\n}\n\n.label {\n  margin: 0 0 6px;\n  font-size: 0.8rem;\n  letter-spacing: 0.08em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: #57738a;\n}\n\nh1 {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: 2rem;\n}\n\n.forecast {\n  border-top: 1px solid #dce6ed;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid #dce6ed;\n  padding: 24px 0;\n  margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n\n#description {\n  margin: 0 0 8px;\n  font-size: 1.2rem;\n}\n\n#tempMain {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: 3rem;\n  font-weight: bold;\n}\n\n.details {\n  margin-bottom: 24px;\n}\n\n.details p {\n  margin: 8px 0;\n}\n\nbutton {\n  width: 100%;\n  padding: 14px 18px;\n  border: none;\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  background: #1f6feb;\n  color: white;\n  font-size: 1rem;\n  font-weight: bold;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\nbutton:hover {\n  background: #185abc;\n}\n\n.hint {\n  margin: 18px 0 0;\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n  line-height: 1.4;\n  color: #57738a;\n}",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "4": {
          "id": "4",
          "name": "script.js",
          "language": "js",
          "contents": "const LAT = \"37.7749\";\nconst LON = \"-122.4194\";\nconst HEADERS = { \"User-Agent\": \"MyWeatherApp/1.0\" };\n\nwindow.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n  fetchNWSWeather();\n\n  const refreshButton = document.getElementById(\"refreshButton\");\n  refreshButton.addEventListener(\"click\", fetchNWSWeather);\n});\n\nconst fetchNWSWeather = async () => {\n  try {\n    setLoadingState();\n\n    const pointsResponse = await fetch(\n      `https://api.weather.gov/points/${LAT},${LON}`,\n      { headers: HEADERS }\n    );\n    const pointsData = await pointsResponse.json();\n\n    const forecastUrl = pointsData.properties.forecast;\n\n    const weatherResponse = await fetch(forecastUrl, { headers: HEADERS });\n    const weatherData = await weatherResponse.json();\n\n    const currentPeriod = weatherData.properties.periods[0];\n    renderUI(currentPeriod);\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Fetch Error:\", error);\n    showErrorState();\n  }\n};\n\nconst setLoadingState = () => {\n  document.getElementById(\"description\").innerText = \"Loading forecast...\";\n  document.getElementById(\"tempMain\").innerText = \"--\";\n  document.getElementById(\"rainChance\").innerText = \"--\";\n  document.getElementById(\"wind\").innerText = \"--\";\n};\n\nconst renderUI = (period) => {\n  document.getElementById(\"cityName\").innerText = \"San Francisco, CA\";\n  document.getElementById(\"description\").innerText = period.shortForecast;\n  document.getElementById(\"tempMain\").innerText =\n    `${period.temperature}°${period.temperatureUnit}`;\n\n  const rainValue = period.probabilityOfPrecipitation?.value || 0;\n  document.getElementById(\"rainChance\").innerText = `${rainValue}%`;\n\n  document.getElementById(\"wind\").innerText =\n    `${period.windSpeed} ${period.windDirection || \"\"}`;\n};\n\nconst showErrorState = () => {\n  document.getElementById(\"description\").innerText = \"Forecast unavailable\";\n  document.getElementById(\"tempMain\").innerText = \"--\";\n  document.getElementById(\"rainChance\").innerText = \"--\";\n  document.getElementById(\"wind\").innerText = \"--\";\n};",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [

      ]
    },
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Watch Live Weather Data\r\n\r\nThis app is already built. It gets live weather data from outside the app.\r\n\r\n#### Do This:\r\n1. Click **Refresh Forecast** and watch what changes in the app.\r\n2. Open the **debug panel** and toggle to **Network**.\r\n3. Click **Refresh Forecast** again.\r\n4. Click around in the Network tab and see what you notice behind the scenes.\r\n\r\nYou do not need to write any code. Just notice how the data in the app connects to the data behind the scenes.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n:::details [**Where do I find the debug panel button?**]\r\nClick the bug icon on the top right of the page. \r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/94dc204b39691b9515108248e0642911-image-1772148344768.25.25 PM.png\" width=\"50\">\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [**Tip:** Drag the debugging panel up to enlarge.]\r\n\r\n![](https://images.code.org/ed2cadce47b2ac42d2a0eb0d516e58dc-image-1783452125689.3267641.gif)\r\n:::\r\n\r\n",
